WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:19.300
Part nine: your own return. Anil Kumar Demo - made up, like everyone in these films - is salaried and holds a few mutual funds. He signed up as an individual, was approved at once, and his one client is himself. He opens My return.

2
00:00:19.921 --> 00:00:28.371
Five steps: gather, check, choose, review and file. Each ticks itself off as it is done.

3
00:00:28.968 --> 00:00:36.718
First, a checklist of what to keep handy. Each line ticks itself as the document comes in.

4
00:00:37.328 --> 00:00:43.378
And where each document comes from: who issues it, and what it gives the return.

5
00:00:44.610 --> 00:00:51.760
He starts with the pre-filled JSON from the e-filing portal. Drop it in, and read it.

6
00:00:52.375 --> 00:01:04.375
Then a Form 16 from each employer, as PDFs: Demo Software, and the academy where he teaches at weekends - another T A N, so a second employer.

7
00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:21.980
The A I S PDF is locked the department's way: his P A N in small letters and his date of birth. He types it once - the eye shows what he typed.

8
00:01:22.593 --> 00:01:44.653
The 26 A S - its Part A 2 shows the buyer of his plot deducted tax under 194 I A. His C A M S capital-gains statement, as the P D F C A M S sends. His bank statement. And last year's I T R 3, for the losses he carried forward.

9
00:01:45.281 --> 00:02:03.901
Every document shows what was read from it: salary and tax deducted from each Form 16, interest and dividends from the A I S, the buyer's tax from the 26 A S, four sales from the C A M S P D F, and the interest in his bank statement.

10
00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:29.099
Later his employer sends a revised Form 16 - the same employer, the same T A N. He is asked first: replace the first one, for a revised Form 16 - or keep both, for two spells with one employer. A Form 16 with another T A N is simply a second employer. Nothing is overwritten without asking.

11
00:02:29.703 --> 00:02:38.293
History keeps it all: each document added, the Form 16 replaced - and the old one kept, ready to download.

12
00:02:38.906 --> 00:02:47.476
At the top, his return at a glance: total income, tax, and the refund due - kept up to date with every document.

13
00:02:48.093 --> 00:02:57.983
Check: each Form 16's tax deducted beside the 26 A S, salary and interest beside the A I S - they agree.

14
00:02:58.625 --> 00:03:15.474
Two employers: each Form 16 took off the standard deduction, and the return takes it once - so expect a little tax to pay. And the 26 A S shows a buyer's tax on a property he has not added yet: the plot, in part ten.

15
00:03:16.093 --> 00:03:21.493
Choose: both regimes worked out in full, and the cheaper one marked.

16
00:03:22.093 --> 00:03:25.833
And from income to tax, step by step.

17
00:03:26.437 --> 00:03:35.967
Next, part ten: the review - capital gains, a plot sold, a flat he co-owns, gifts - and the return, ready to file.
